{"name":"Hog Bristle","hex":"#dcd1bb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hog","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any animal belonging to the Suidae family of mammals, especially the pig, the warthog, and the boar.\n An adult swine, at or above a certain body weight.","An adult swine, at or above a certain body weight."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To greedily take more than one's share, to take precedence at the expense of another or others.","To clip the mane of a horse, making it short and bristly.\n\n (of a hedge) to trim up closely"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hog"},{"term":"bristle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A stiff or coarse hair on a nonhuman mammal or on a plant.","A chaeta: an analogous filament on arthropods, annelids, or other animals."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To rise or stand erect, like bristles.","To abound, to be covered with, or to have an abundance of, something, especially something jutting out."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bristle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Paintbrush","blocks":[{"text":"A paintbrush is a brush used to apply paint or ink. A paintbrush is usually made by clamping bristles to a handle with a ferrule. They are available in various sizes, shapes, and materials. Thicker ones are used for filling in, and thinner ones are used for details. They may be subdivided into decorators' brushes used for painting and decorating and artists' brushes used for visual art."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Paintbrushes.jpg/330px-Paintbrushes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paintbrush","wikidata":"Q193897"},{"title":"Bristle","blocks":[{"text":"A bristle is a stiff hair or feather, either on an animal, such as a pig, a plant, or on a tool such as a brush or broom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Brushbristles.jpg/330px-Brushbristles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bristle","wikidata":"Q894231"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Parts_of_a_Paintbrush.png/120px-Parts_of_a_Paintbrush.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a0/Parts_of_a_Paintbrush.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Parts_of_a_Paintbrush.png/120px-Parts_of_a_Paintbrush.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brush parts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParts_of_a_Paintbrush.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Brush_Handles.jpg/500px-Brush_Handles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Brush_Handles.jpg/1280px-Brush_Handles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Brush_Handles.jpg/500px-Brush_Handles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brush handle styles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrush_Handles.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Decorators%27paintbiushes.jpg/500px-Decorators%27paintbiushes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Decorators%27paintbiushes.jpg/1280px-Decorators%27paintbiushes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Decorators%27paintbiushes.jpg/500px-Decorators%27paintbiushes.jpg?ut